.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-restore-raw-volume 1  "tapectl-restore-raw-volume " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-restore\-raw\-volume \- Dump every file off a tape verbatim, using only what is on the tape itself (no database needed) — the emergency/heir path. \-\-positions and \-\-only narrow it to the files named (a full cartridge is a terabyte; RESTORE.sh alone is `\-\-only restore_sh`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl restore raw\-volume\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-positions\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dump every file off a tape verbatim, using only what is on the tape itself (no database needed) — the emergency/heir path. \-\-positions and \-\-only narrow it to the files named (a full cartridge is a terabyte; RESTORE.sh alone is `\-\-only restore_sh`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination directory
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Refuse unless the tape\*(Aqs own reported label matches (wrong\-tape guard) — not a database lookup
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-positions\fR \fI<N>\fR
Dump only the files at these tape positions (comma\-separated or repeated; File 0 is the ID thunk, 2 RESTORE.sh, 3 the front index). With \-\-only, a file either names is dumped
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR
Dump only the files of these front\-index types (comma\-separated or repeated): id_thunk, system_guide, restore_sh, front_index, tenant_envelope, operator_envelope, operator_envelope_backup, data_slice, seal_marker
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
